---
import '../styles/global.css';
---
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="description" content="Draft framework: Samoa climate variability data story." />
    <title>The Year We Plan For — Draft framework</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <header class="hero wrap">
        <p class="eyebrow">PACIFIC DATAVIZ CHALLENGE 2026 · DRAFT FRAMEWORK</p>
        <h1>The Year We Plan For</h1>
        <p class="standfirst">Samoa’s rain, heat and the decisions between them.</p>
        <p class="dek">This framework makes one limited point: resilience cannot be planned around an average year. It shows observed national rainfall variability alongside sea-surface-temperature context — without predicting local water security or claiming causation.</p>
      </header>
      <section class="signal wrap" aria-labelledby="question">
        <p class="section-label">THE QUESTION</p>
        <h2 id="question">What changes when a climate plan is tested against the years Samoa has already experienced?</h2>
        <p>National data can show context and variability. It cannot decide what an individual village, catchment or household needs. Local evidence and consent remain an evidence gate.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="wrap story-section" aria-labelledby="rain-title">
        <div class="section-intro"><p class="section-label">01 · VARIABILITY</p><h2 id="rain-title">The average year is not the year people plan for.</h2><p>Annual precipitation anomalies, relative to the official 1991–2020 reference period. Bars show measured anomaly; fine lines show reported standard error.</p></div>
        <div id="rainfall-chart" class="chart" aria-label="Annual Samoa precipitation anomalies chart"></div>
        <p class="caption">Observed annual national aggregate. A negative bar is below the reference average; it is not a local drought declaration.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="wrap story-section paired" aria-labelledby="sst-title">
        <div class="section-intro"><p class="section-label">02 · CONTEXT</p><h2 id="sst-title">The ocean backdrop is not static.</h2><p>Annual Samoa EEZ sea-surface-temperature anomalies, relative to the official 1971–2000 reference period.</p></div>
        <div id="sst-chart" class="chart" aria-label="Annual Samoa sea surface temperature anomaly chart"></div>
        <p class="caption">This is an EEZ aggregate, not a coastal or inshore temperature record. It is displayed alongside rainfall for context, not as proof of a causal relationship.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="wrap cards" aria-labelledby="gate-title">
        <p class="section-label">03 · BEFORE ANY FORECAST</p><h2 id="gate-title">Evidence gates for the next build</h2>
        <article><h3>Seasonal preparedness</h3><p>Add a below/near/above-normal outlook only when an authoritative product and its hindcast skill are documented.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Food resilience</h3><p>Add a selected crop only after provenance and interpretation have been checked. Correlation must not become a causal claim.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Local decisions</h3><p>Add station, catchment or community detail only with authorised data, quality metadata and, where relevant, local review.</p></article>
      </section>
      <section class="wrap methods">
        <h2>What this draft does not do</h2>
        <ul><li>Forecast water-system failure, disaster impacts or crop yields.</li><li>Rank villages or communities.</li><li>Convert missing data into zeroes.</li><li>Use a single number to define “resilience”.</li></ul>
        <p>Sources and limitations: <a href="https://stats-sdmx-disseminate.pacificdata.org/rest/data/SPC,DF_CLIMATE_CHANGE,1.0/A.RAIN_ANOM.WS?dimensionAtObservation=AllDimensions">SPC rainfall SDMX</a> · <a href="https://stats-sdmx-disseminate.pacificdata.org/rest/data/SPC,DF_CLIMATE_CHANGE,1.0/A.SST_ANOM.WS?dimensionAtObservation=AllDimensions">SPC SST SDMX</a> · <a href="https://pacificdatavizchallenge.org/">Challenge data catalogue</a>.</p>
      </section>
    </main>
    <script>
      import * as Plot from '@observablehq/plot';
      type Row = [number, number, number];
      type Data = { rainfall: Row[]; sst: Row[] };
      const data = await fetch('/data/samoa-climate.json').then((r) => r.json()) as Data;
      const rainfall = data.rainfall.map(([year, anomaly, se]) => ({year, anomaly, se}));
      const sst = data.sst.map(([year, anomaly, se]) => ({year, anomaly, se}));
      const mount = (id: string, chart: SVGSVGElement | HTMLElement) => document.querySelector(`#${id}`)?.append(chart);
      mount('rainfall-chart', Plot.plot({
        width: 960, height: 350, marginLeft: 58, marginBottom: 42, grid: true,
        x: {label: 'Year', ticks: 10}, y: {label: 'Precipitation anomaly (mm)'},
        marks: [Plot.ruleY([0], {stroke: '#1d323a'}), Plot.ruleX(rainfall, {x:'year', y1:d=>d.anomaly-d.se, y2:d=>d.anomaly+d.se, stroke:'#697b81'}), Plot.barY(rainfall, {x:'year', y:'anomaly', fill:d=>d.anomaly < 0 ? '#ba6d3c' : '#236a86', title:d => `${d.year}: ${d.anomaly} mm (SE ${d.se} mm)`})]
      }));
      mount('sst-chart', Plot.plot({
        width: 960, height: 350, marginLeft: 58, marginBottom: 42, grid: true,
        x: {label: 'Year', ticks: 10}, y: {label: 'SST anomaly (°C)'},
        marks: [Plot.ruleY([0], {stroke: '#1d323a'}), Plot.lineY(sst, {x:'year', y:'anomaly', stroke:'#c24129', strokeWidth:2.5, title:d => `${d.year}: ${d.anomaly} °C (SE ${d.se} °C)`}), Plot.dot(sst, {x:'year', y:'anomaly', fill:'#c24129', r:2.5})]
      }));
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
